  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8477;</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8477;</mi></math>&nbsp;be defined as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"\"><mtable columnalign=\"left\"><mtr><mtd><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup></mfenced><mo>,</mo></mtd><mtd><mi>x</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>2</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo></mtd><mtd><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>2</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math><br />where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>&#8477;</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>t</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;denotes greatest integer less than or equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math>. Then, which of the following statements is true?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "wlZP1",
      "text": "There exists <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8477;</mi></math>&nbsp;such that&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi></math> is continuous of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8477;</mi></math>.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "DC3Y4",
      "text": "If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi></math>&nbsp;is discontinuous at exactly one point, then&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "vCsYC",
      "text": "If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi></math>&nbsp;is discontinuous at exactly one point, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>1</mn></math>.",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "P1zUJ",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi></math>&nbsp;is discontinuous at atleast two points, for any values of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi></math>.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
